entry.summary:
"We want to escape Excel hell too... how should we start?" I get this question frequently. A startup CTO shared this: It's not funny, but this is reality. While helping multiple teams migrate, I realized something. Changing tools is easier than changing people's habits. First, we need to measure how dependent our team is on Excel. Excel Dependency Index (EDI): # How dependent is our team on Excel? edi_factors = { "Excel files": 47, # count "Weekly updates": 120, # times "Related people": 15, # people "Macros/VBA": True, # exists "External integrations": 5, # count "Usage period": 36 # months }
# EDI score calculation score = (files × 2) + (updates × 3) + (people × 2) + ...
# Result interpretation…
